{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053918-cross-genre-relationships","id":1053918,"title":"Cross-Genre Relationships?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-23T11:38:26-08:00","id":1053918,"title":"Cross-Genre Relationships?","content":"I just wanted to ask if anyone has had any experience with or has any advice about cross-genre relationships on multi-genre boards (I'm on a board that has WtA, VtM, Mage, and regular mortals in the oWoD setting). My Metis Garou is currently in a relationship/having a fling with a Mage (both are so far unaware of the other's supernatural nature; the Mage feels his Rage, of course, but is still interested, and he hasn't put the dots together yet about this human woman he likes). I guess my questions are: Is it just a bad idea all-around or can it work? Do the characters have to remain ignorant of each other's natures for it to work? What kind of repercussions could there be if the relationship is discovered, etc? I'm asking in general, not just the specifics of my own character's situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12788,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12788-ruadhan","user":"Ruadhan","date":". 02-23-2017, 02:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12788-ruadhan","name":"Ruadhan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T11:55:15-08:00","id":1053929,"title":"","content":"Lucky lucky Terje!<br /> <br /> Anyway, to me crossover worked best like this: Low-level characters/pariahs in general, no direct contact to higher society. And no dice. As in, things are kept at personal levels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T12:08:19-08:00","id":1053935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053918-cross-genre-relationships?p=1053929#post1053929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lucky lucky Terje!<br /> <br /> Anyway, to me crossover worked best like this: Low-level characters/pariahs in general, no direct contact to higher society. And no dice. As in, things are kept at personal levels.</div> </div> </div> </div>LOL Yes. By that, do you mean they should just keep the relationship a secret?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12788-ruadhan","name":"Ruadhan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T12:31:44-08:00","id":1053945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ruadhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053918-cross-genre-relationships?p=1053935#post1053935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> LOL Yes. By that, do you mean they should just keep the relationship a secret?</div> </div> </div> </div>Talk to the STs, but generally if they don't -know- what the other is, let thing advance how they may.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T15:28:06-08:00","id":1054963,"title":"","content":"Thanks! Anyone else want to chime in also? I'm also interested in the question as it applies generally. Has anyone seen cross-genre relationships on their board? How did it work out?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12788-ruadhan","name":"Ruadhan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T15:46:50-08:00","id":1054968,"title":"","content":"Yes, I have seen Changeling-Fera relationships, and they tend to work out because of the strange interfertility of the two groups. With a Metis, the rest of the Garou will probably just shake their head sadly, but it is not like he is bothering a female Kinfolk, so they will probably not care. Now, if they find out that she is a Mage, that will probably change things, but she is honestly unlikely to reveal her true nature. <br /> <br /> Since she cannot ever have Garou or Kinfolk children with her Metis lover, she will never really be in a position to betray the Veil, so no one will care. The real complicating factor becomes if she is one of the lost Kinfolk and another Garou sniffs her out. If that happens, the elders may force the Metis to end the relationship so another Garou has a chance to put a bun in the oven, so to speak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T16:09:53-08:00","id":1054977,"title":"","content":"That is very helpful, thank you! I guess my next question is: If she does reveal that she is a Mage, does he have to then end the relationship since Mages are a potential enemy who can deplete a caern? vs. If he decided to continue the relationship in secret anyway even though he knows she's a Mage, is he just setting himself up for major trouble if the other Garou found out? Just wondering what the repercussions would be. I feel like a Mage isn't on the same level as a vampire, but I am new and I really don't know. Also, just out of curiosity, if he was a Homid Garou, would things be very different since he could potentially get her pregnant? Can Garou have Kinfolk or Garou children with a regular human, the chances are just way lower than with a Kinfolk?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12788,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12788-ruadhan","user":"Ruadhan","date":". 02-25-2017, 07:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12788-ruadhan","name":"Ruadhan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T18:22:37-08:00","id":1055023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ruadhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053918-cross-genre-relationships?p=1054977#post1054977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is very helpful, thank you! I guess my next question is: If she does reveal that she is a Mage, does he have to then end the relationship since Mages are a potential enemy who can deplete a caern? vs. If he decided to continue the relationship in secret anyway even though he knows she's a Mage, is he just setting himself up for major trouble if the other Garou found out? Just wondering what the repercussions would be. I feel like a Mage isn't on the same level as a vampire, but I am new and I really don't know.</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends on the Tribal make up of the Sept and history of the sept along with the Tradition/Craft/Convention of the mage their history in the local area. Along with how much Renown you have, and how you spin the story to others. &quot;I'm seducing this potential enemy and keeping her away from the sept and directing her at our enemies aren't I super fucking clever shadowlord?&quot; for example is an option.<br /> <br /> So your character is a Metis, what Tribe? A Child of Gaia might be able to argue love but a Shadowlord knows love is weakness so he needs a better argument.<br /> <br /> Presumably the Mage isn't a Technocrat or Nephandi but a &quot;standard&quot; mage those on the more naturalistic end can work quite effectively with Garou and be powerful allies. But even some of the more techno focused types can play nice with Glasswalkers.<br /> <br /> Has the Sept in the past had serious issues with Mages or is there more &quot;they are potentially dangerous&quot;? A Caern who's had to fight off a bunch of Mage assaults is going to treat the situation different than one that hasn't had a history with mages except via vague commentary on them.<br /> <br /> <br /> All secrets are eventually uncovered. How it comes out will effect the situation. Even &quot;I left her after discovering she was a Mage&quot; will potentially have people questioning your actions.<br /> <br /> [quote[Also, just out of curiosity, if he was a Homid Garou, would things be very different since he could potentially get her pregnant? Can Garou have Kinfolk or Garou children with a regular human, the chances are just way lower than with a Kinfolk?[/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> Yes to all of the above. If your character were Lupus the same would be true too. Breeds TEND to stick to theirown kin but its not manditory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T18:46:42-08:00","id":1055027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053918-cross-genre-relationships?p=1055023#post1055023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It depends on the Tribal make up of the Sept and history of the sept along with the Tradition/Craft/Convention of the mage their history in the local area. Along with how much Renown you have, and how you spin the story to others. &quot;I'm seducing this potential enemy and keeping her away from the sept and directing her at our enemies aren't I super fucking clever shadowlord?&quot; for example is an option.<br /> <br /> So your character is a Metis, what Tribe? A Child of Gaia might be able to argue love but a Shadowlord knows love is weakness so he needs a better argument.<br /> <br /> Presumably the Mage isn't a Technocrat or Nephandi but a &quot;standard&quot; mage those on the more naturalistic end can work quite effectively with Garou and be powerful allies. But even some of the more techno focused types can play nice with Glasswalkers.<br /> <br /> Has the Sept in the past had serious issues with Mages or is there more &quot;they are potentially dangerous&quot;? A Caern who's had to fight off a bunch of Mage assaults is going to treat the situation different than one that hasn't had a history with mages except via vague commentary on them.<br /> <br /> <br /> All secrets are eventually uncovered. How it comes out will effect the situation. Even &quot;I left her after discovering she was a Mage&quot; will potentially have people questioning your actions.<br /> <br /> [quote[Also, just out of curiosity, if he was a Homid Garou, would things be very different since he could potentially get her pregnant? Can Garou have Kinfolk or Garou children with a regular human, the chances are just way lower than with a Kinfolk?<br /> <br /> Yes to all of the above. If your character were Lupus the same would be true too. Breeds TEND to stick to theirown kin but its not manditory.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, from what I have read of the history of the area that was posted, the Mages have pretty much stayed out of conflict with the other supernaturals throughout their long history and have until recent times been pretty isolationist. What attacks there have been on the Sept have come from forces of the Wyrm (which are not specified). My character is a relatively new arrival at the Sept and has not really established himself there yet.<br /> <br /> I know this will probably sound crazy, but he is Get of Fenris. However, he's not entirely played straight as a Get of Fenris. He is a fierce warrior, but he can also be more compassionate than might be usual with a Fenrir.<br /> <br /> The Mage is Verbena and seems to enjoy nature and basically being a Pagan witch. Does not come across as a threat at all nor does she seem to be doing anything nefarious. They seem to have a genuine connection. I'm just wondering how to play it if he does find out she's a Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12788,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12788-ruadhan","user":"Ruadhan","date":". 02-25-2017, 10:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12788-ruadhan","name":"Ruadhan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T19:09:02-08:00","id":1055037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ruadhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053918-cross-genre-relationships?p=1055027#post1055027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, from what I have read of the history of the area that was posted, the Mages have pretty much stayed out of conflict with the other supernaturals throughout their long history and have until recent times been pretty isolationist. What attacks there have been on the Sept have come from forces of the Wyrm (which are not specified).<br /> <br /> I know this will probably sound crazy, but he is Get of Fenris. However, he's not entirely played straight as a Get of Fenris. He is a fierce warrior, but he can also be more compassionate than might be usual with a Fenrir.<br /> <br /> The Mage is Verbena and seems to enjoy nature and basically being a Pagan witch. Does not come across as a threat at all nor does she seem to be doing anything nefarious.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Doesn't sound Crazy at all. You've proven yourself to Fenris. What auspice are you? Is she Norse Pagan(that can be a problem since they worship many things that the Fenrir equate with the wyrm)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T19:38:35-08:00","id":1055042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053918-cross-genre-relationships?p=1055037#post1055037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Doesn't sound Crazy at all. You've proven yourself to Fenris. What auspice are you? Is she Norse Pagan(that can be a problem since they worship many things that the Fenrir equate with the wyrm)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> He is an Ahroun. She doesn't seem to be Norse Pagan, more like your standard neopagan/sort of Wiccan/druidic. What do you think about if he learns she is a Mage? Does that make him duty-bound to leave her or else he'd be in major trouble with the other Garou, even if the Mage means no harm to the Garou and the caern?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12788-ruadhan","name":"Ruadhan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T20:00:32-08:00","id":1055052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ruadhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053918-cross-genre-relationships?p=1055042#post1055042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> He is an Ahroun. She doesn't seem to be Norse Pagan, more like your standard neopagan/sort of Wiccan/druidic. What do you think about if he learns she is a Mage? Does that make him duty-bound to leave her or else he'd be in major trouble with the other Garou, even if the Mage means no harm to the Garou and the caern?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mages can pose a threat to caerns, drinking them dry of spirit power to fuel their own magic, but... she wouldn't do that, right? <i>She's different.</i><br /> <br /> As far as you having to drop her like a hot potato upon finding that she was a will-worker, I think it depends on you as an individual. Mages are more compatible with Garou than, say, vampires or demons, and coexistence is possible. Heck, in my game, one of my Garou was unwittingly adopted by a mage. Things were tense after her first change, although they still exchange letters and she thinks of him as a distant father figure. He has come to her aid in the past when she was in a jam, even if the other Garou are mistrustful of his motives.<br /> <br /> I think the less the Wiccan-wizard knows, the safer the relationship is. Don't let her know where the caern is, if possible, because even if she means no harm, her buddies might have no such qualms... and the last thing you want to do is be accused of risking a caern, especially if you are kind of an outsider.<br /> <br /> I also think things might be rough for your Metis if this came to light, just because Metis get the short end of the stick, but if you can handle the potential fallout, go after that magic pussy. It is dangerous, but the story seems interesting. Forbidden love is the sort of stuff that a good storyteller can really work with. I can also see the appeal of a Metis being drawn to an illicit relationship, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 02-25-2017, 11:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T20:15:58-08:00","id":1055058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ruadhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053918-cross-genre-relationships?p=1055042#post1055042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> He is an Ahroun. She doesn't seem to be Norse Pagan, more like your standard neopagan/sort of Wiccan/druidic. What do you think about if he learns she is a Mage? Does that make him duty-bound to leave her or else he'd be in major trouble with the other Garou, even if the Mage means no harm to the Garou and the caern?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Well a ragabash would have more latitude to interpret things but you make do. Generally speaking your Duty is to Gaia. Then your tribe. Then somewhat last there yourself. Your tribe is going to treat any romantic interactions you have as recreational because you can't have kids. Now you might be tempted down the path of &quot;maybe Magick can fix this&quot; don't go down that path mages have been around forever and no one else has ever tried? clearly there's a reason.<br /> <br /> As a Verbena she's unlikely to be an enemy of Gaia, your Tribe MIGHT have issues with the situation.. but you'd also get a situation for having a relationship with.. ANYONE its a betrayal its wasting your time, you have more important things to do. It has alot of potential to blow up on your face.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T22:02:19-08:00","id":1055087,"title":"","content":"If he was non-Metis (Homid or Lupus), he would have a 10% chance of siring Homid Garou and 90% chance of siring Human Kinfolk. Mating with Kinfolk only improves the odds if they have Pure Breed (5% per level). The primary reason why Garou mate with Kinfolk is that they already know the secret and are immune to Delirium.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T22:09:10-08:00","id":1055088,"title":"","content":"I agree with The Laughing Stranger that it makes for an interesting, if potentially dangerous story. So far we've been enjoying writing this story together. the Mage and I. I guess I'll just have to wait and see how things develop. It just seems like a shame that the one thing that the Metis gets to enjoy could kill him or land him in very hot water. Dude can't catch a break, no matter what.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12788-ruadhan","name":"Ruadhan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T22:23:47-08:00","id":1055094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ruadhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053918-cross-genre-relationships?p=1055088#post1055088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with The Laughing Stranger that it makes for an interesting, if potentially dangerous story. So far we've been enjoying writing this story together. the Mage and I. I guess I'll just have to wait and see how things develop. It just seems like a shame that the one thing that the Metis gets to enjoy could kill him or land him in very hot water. Dude can't catch a break, no matter what.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, your Ahroun does have the saving grace of being in a tribe where might (if not necessarily making right) certainly gives you a lot more leeway than he'd otherwise have. If anyone other than an elder gives you guff, stare them down, or if you are feeling particularly angry, challenge them and wipe the floor with their ass. As you said, it is one of the few sources of joy for the poor bastard. That is worth protecting.<br /> <br /> What deformity does your Full Moon suffer from?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 02-26-2017, 01:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T22:37:51-08:00","id":1055096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053918-cross-genre-relationships?p=1055094#post1055094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, your Ahroun does have the saving grace of being in a tribe where might (if not necessarily making right) certainly gives you a lot more leeway than he'd otherwise have. If anyone other than an elder gives you guff, stare them down, or if you are feeling particularly angry, challenge them and wipe the floor with their ass. As you said, it is one of the few sources of joy for the poor bastard. That is worth protecting.<br /> <br /> What deformity does your Full Moon suffer from?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Very well said! It is certainly worth protecting. I keep forgetting I have the &quot;kick ass&quot; option. His deformity is Bestial Reflection, so he reflects his breed form in all reflective surfaces, like glass, so he can't go into the local city and pick up chicks. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12788-ruadhan","name":"Ruadhan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T22:44:44-08:00","id":1055097,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ruadhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053918-cross-genre-relationships?p=1055096#post1055096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I keep forgetting I have the &quot;kick ass&quot; option.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just don't bite off more than you can chew and the Metis should be fine for now. Not sure what the tribal makeup of your current sept is, but most Get kinda appreciate ass-kicking. After a few brawls your character might have earned more friends than foes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> His deformity is Bestial Reflection, so he reflects his breed form in all reflective surfaces, like glass, so he can't go into the local city and pick up chicks. :P </div> </div> </div>Interesting... there is some potential for drama even in your flaw. I like it. Let us know how it goes!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T11:07:12-08:00","id":1055318,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I am still learning the ropes and can be a bit too cautious as a player, which is why he hasn't gotten into a fight with anyone yet. Something to work on and use judiciously. There is a Get of Fenris NPC pack among the other packs at the Sept. He is one of 2 Get of Fenris PCs. So I guess some at the Sept would appreciate some brawling.<br /> <br /> As long as she doesn't whip out a mirror on him, I think he's safe for now. :P But could provide some nice drama later.<br /> <br /> I will! Thank you everyone for your replies! They were very helpful! :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12788,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12788-ruadhan","user":"Ruadhan","date":". 02-26-2017, 02:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12788-ruadhan","name":"Ruadhan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T13:39:50-08:00","id":1055371,"title":"","content":"What about a reflection in water or a store window?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T14:23:54-08:00","id":1055389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053918-cross-genre-relationships?p=1055371#post1055371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about a reflection in water or a store window?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh, yes, that's right. The store windows and such are why he can't go into the city or even the Kinfolk town. Yes, a stream would be an issue if he and the Mage came upon one (they see each other in the forest in a state park). He'd have to contrive a way to avoid going close enough to the stream to show a reflection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12788-ruadhan","name":"Ruadhan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T14:33:52-08:00","id":1055391,"title":"","content":"It is a bitter-sweet relationship because he 'knows' that she cannot accept the truth of his nature. Since he does not know of her nature, he 'knows' that his very reflection would cause the Delirium in her. <br /> <br /> Because he cannot sire children on her, he cannot even hope for magic that would turn her into Kinfolk (making her immune to the Delirium) because the elders of his Sept would not waste such magic on the lover of a Metis because the Sept gains nothing from his relationship. Of course, the Metis could attempt an Umbra quest to gain such magic from an Incarna, but the cost would be high, and his beloved would be encouraged to mate with another so she could bear Garou or Kinfolk.<br /> <br /> Of course, what would be her reaction if she discovered that she slept with a monster? Would she run away screaming? Would she accept him? Would she undergo an Umbra quest to have herself transformed from a Mage into a Garou, not understanding the difficulty or the consequences of such an action?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T14:46:28-08:00","id":1055398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053918-cross-genre-relationships?p=1055058#post1055058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well a ragabash would have more latitude to interpret things but you make do. Generally speaking your Duty is to Gaia. Then your tribe. Then somewhat last there yourself. Your tribe is going to treat any romantic interactions you have as recreational because you can't have kids. Now you might be tempted down the path of &quot;maybe Magick can fix this&quot; don't go down that path mages have been around forever and no one else has ever tried? clearly there's a reason.<br /> <br /> As a Verbena she's unlikely to be an enemy of Gaia, your Tribe MIGHT have issues with the situation.. but you'd also get a situation for having a relationship with.. ANYONE its a betrayal its wasting your time, you have more important things to do. It has alot of potential to blow up on your face.</div> </div> </div> </div>A mage with life and spirit(both the most likely spheres for a verbena will have) probably can make metis fertile. Though based on how you interpret the metis infertility thing(if it's a curse from gaia, or a generic/spirit querk similar to inbreeding) it could still have dire, weird, or no consiquence.<br /> <br /> You could treat it as a normal permanent effect and give said metic a permanent paradox flaw, The magic could just fail and cause an automatic backlash, or it could work swimmingly with everyone happy(does pose the question of whether the child would be homid or metis though.)<br /> <br /> Besides if neither is aware of the other's nature, it'll be more likely that said magical girlfriend finds out our veritable bachaler is infertile(and if she wants kids) she'll probably try to slip in a little magic and call it a miracle to our new (and confused) father. Though the sept finding out about a woman who can have kids with metis is a can of worms in itself(likely involving a kidnapping and a garou pack leader screaming something about a gift from gaia)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T14:57:11-08:00","id":1055403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053918-cross-genre-relationships?p=1055398#post1055398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides if neither is aware of the other's nature, it'll be more likely that said magical girlfriend finds out our veritable bachaler is infertile(and if she wants kids) she'll probably try to slip in a little magic and call it a miracle to our new (and confused) father. Though the sept finding out about a woman who can have kids with metis is a can of worms in itself(likely involving a kidnapping and a garou pack leader screaming something about a gift from gaia)</div> </div> </div> </div>This...would go SO badly. If I was the metis player, my first response would be to roll rage. Because obviously the kid isn't mine and my supposedly trustworthy girlfriend is cheating on me. <br /> <br /> And if somehow, that situation doesn't end in death for the mage, obviously the couple will each find out about the other's secret. Now you have to deal with Garou Society bullshit and maybe (depending on how cruel your ST is) crazy supernatural baby bullshit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T15:38:22-08:00","id":1055418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053918-cross-genre-relationships?p=1055403#post1055403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This...would go SO badly. If I was the metis player, my first response would be to roll rage. Because obviously the kid isn't mine and my supposedly trustworthy girlfriend is cheating on me.<br /> <br /> And if somehow, that situation doesn't end in death for the mage, obviously the couple will each find out about the other's secret. Now you have to deal with Garou Society bullshit and maybe (depending on how cruel your ST is) crazy supernatural baby bullshit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. Besides, if she's not crafty enough to think up a scenario to help that magick go along, she's a pretty craptastic mage. (&quot;My great-great-grandmother had this herbal recipe that worked with her husband! Can't we at least try? My family's been doing this kind of herbalism stuff for generations.&quot; I mean, c'mon, that was at the drop of a hat. With some decent planning, she could cook up something pretty good.) If he agrees, great! If he doesn't agree, or if she just doesn't tell him, and she pulls some kind of magick anyway, well... That's just messed up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12777-wakuwa","name":"Wakuwa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12777_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T15:49:01-08:00","id":1055422,"title":"","content":"The metis fertility thing will not end well. Aside from Rage across Australia, the only time any metis was fertile is when creating the perfect metis. Aka, herald of the apocalypse. Even the spontaneous metis from Chernobyl still have non-metis parents.<br /> <br /> At best, the child will be born in crinos. At worst, it has even more deformities than the parent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T17:07:39-08:00","id":1055455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wakuwa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053918-cross-genre-relationships?p=1055418#post1055418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agreed. Besides, if she's not crafty enough to think up a scenario to help that magick go along, she's a pretty craptastic mage. (&quot;My great-great-grandmother had this herbal recipe that worked with her husband! Can't we at least try? My family's been doing this kind of herbalism stuff for generations.&quot; I mean, c'mon, that was at the drop of a hat. With some decent planning, she could cook up something pretty good.) If he agrees, great! If he doesn't agree, or if she just doesn't tell him, and she pulls some kind of magick anyway, well... That's just messed up.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't mean said mage wouldn't come up with some priar reasoning(even if he was human, explaining sudden babies would be complicated relationship wise and paradox wise), just I don't think the metis(who grou society have likely tried many times over many generations to cure and failed) would believe said herbal potion would work, but would try it out to humor his girl. And a DNA test would prove the child was his(which may further complicate matters anyway with garou)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053918-cross-genre-relationships?p=1055422#post1055422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The metis fertility thing will not end well. Aside from Rage across Australia, the only time any metis was fertile is when creating the perfect metis. Aka, herald of the apocalypse. Even the spontaneous metis from Chernobyl still have non-metis parents.<br /> <br /> At best, the child will be born in crinos. At worst, it has even more deformities than the parent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or be born a bygone rather than a werewolf. Or possibly be subject to paradox flaws as a living work of magic. or spontaniously combust.<br /> <br /> This is the WOD we're talking about, but at the same time we're also talking about mages here(who take the words &quot;No you can't/shouldn't&quot; as a challenge). As far as ms. mage knows her hubby is a normal(if angry) guy with fertility issues, if it comes to the point they want kids it would be just a simple potion sip away for her. I'm not saying it will go well, I'm saying it could happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6383,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","user":"Prometheas","date":". 02-26-2017, 08:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T17:26:50-08:00","id":1055461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053918-cross-genre-relationships?p=1055455#post1055455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I didn't mean said mage wouldn't come up with some priar reasoning(even if he was human, explaining sudden babies would be complicated relationship wise and paradox wise), just I don't think the metis(who grou society have likely tried many times over many generations to cure and failed) would believe said herbal potion would work, but would try it out to humor his girl. And a DNA test would prove the child was his(which may further complicate matters anyway with garou)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I could totally see this happening. &quot;It's not going to work anyways, so why not.&quot;<br /> <br /> Still would be a rage roll anyways. Because the Metis KNOWS it isn't his child. <br /> <br /> You know what I would do as ST? I think I would have the child be born a normal human. Not Kinfolk. Not Garou. Not Metis. Not crazy freak monster baby. Just a normal Delerium prone human baby.<br /> <br /> A human baby is what the mage is expecting to happen and isn't Mage about imposing your will on reality? The situation would freak out the metis even more. And maybe cause paradox, because HE knows that shouldn't happen. <br /> <br /> Note, I don't know much about Mage, so correct me if my assumptions are wrong. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T17:39:00-08:00","id":1055467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053918-cross-genre-relationships?p=1055461#post1055461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I could totally see this happening. &quot;It's not going to work anyways, so why not.&quot;<br /> <br /> Still would be a rage roll anyways. Because the Metis KNOWS it isn't his child.<br /> <br /> You know what I would do as ST? I think I would have the child be born a normal human. Not Kinfolk. Not Garou. Not Metis. Not crazy freak monster baby. Just a normal Delerium prone human baby.<br /> <br /> A human baby is what the mage is expecting to happen and isn't Mage about imposing your will on reality? The situation would freak out the metis even more. And maybe cause paradox, because HE knows that shouldn't happen.<br /> <br /> Note, I don't know much about Mage, so correct me if my assumptions are wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not super tuned into Mage either, but I don't think supernatural beasties cause paradox. Mages do impose their will on reality, but unless they are Mauraders, accidentally making your baby human instead of Garou or Kinfolk is kinda off the rez, as far as the rules are concerned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T17:43:04-08:00","id":1055470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053918-cross-genre-relationships?p=1055467#post1055467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not super tuned into Mage either, but I don't think supernatural beasties cause paradox. Mages do impose their will on reality, but unless they are Mauraders, accidentally making your baby human instead of Garou or Kinfolk is kinda off the rez, as far as the rules are concerned.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Maybe I'm confusing Banality with Paradox.<br /> <br /> Making any sort of offspring with a Metis is kinda off the rez though, so why not go so far into crazy you swing back around in to normal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T17:49:13-08:00","id":1055473,"title":"","content":"Well, I think that 'Gaia says no' and the Mage gains 10,000 points of Paradox for trying to circumvent Gaia's prohibitions against Metis's reproducing (only a Supernal like the Wyrm seems to be able to avoid that fate). If Mages could just cure Metis infertility, the Garou would try to get along with Mages better. Of course, the only thing the Metis realizes is that his lady love is annihilated in an explosion that takes out a small city (assuming he was not in the vicinity)..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T17:54:24-08:00","id":1055477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053918-cross-genre-relationships?p=1055470#post1055470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Making any sort of offspring with a Metis is kinda off the rez though, so why not go so far into crazy you swing back around in to normal.</div> </div> </div> </div>True that- and there is nothing to say momma mage couldn't cast some kinda spell on the unborn kid. It just wouldn't be a surprise is all.<br /> <br /> Supernatural relationships are weird things, yo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T17:57:09-08:00","id":1055479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053918-cross-genre-relationships?p=1055473#post1055473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I think that 'Gaia says no' and the Mage gains 10,000 points of Paradox for trying to circumvent Gaia's prohibitions against Metis's reproducing (only a Supernal like the Wyrm seems to be able to avoid that fate). If Mages could just cure Metis infertility, the Garou would try to get along with Mages better. Of course, the only thing the Metis realizes is that his lady love is annihilated in an explosion that takes out a small city (assuming he was not in the vicinity)..</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't think the Garou Nation is going to start courting mages if the outcome of this spell is &quot;Non-Kin Non-Garou baby&quot;. Gaia has enough of those pesky humans around, no need for Metis to make more. <br /> <br /> To be honest, I'd probably say &quot;Nope. It doesn't work&quot; if the situation came up in one of my games. I was just shooting shit to see what other outcomes I could come up with besides &quot;Horrible monster baby.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T18:30:13-08:00","id":1055491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053918-cross-genre-relationships?p=1055470#post1055470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Maybe I'm confusing Banality with Paradox.<br /> <br /> Making any sort of offspring with a Metis is kinda off the rez though, so why not go so far into crazy you swing back around in to normal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the only mages powerful enough to unknowingly change reality are mauraders and archmages. Reality is sorta predetermened by consensus and/or spirit's messing with something. So unless the mage actively tried to make the baby human it would most likely be kinfolk.<br /> <br /> Though story-wise it's an interesting concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T22:40:15-08:00","id":1055547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053918-cross-genre-relationships?p=1055473#post1055473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I think that 'Gaia says no' and the Mage gains 10,000 points of Paradox for trying to circumvent Gaia's prohibitions against Metis's reproducing (only a Supernal like the Wyrm seems to be able to avoid that fate). If Mages could just cure Metis infertility, the Garou would try to get along with Mages better. Of course, the only thing the Metis realizes is that his lady love is annihilated in an explosion that takes out a small city (assuming he was not in the vicinity)..</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I find &quot;a BILLLLION POINTS OF PARADOX&quot; the boring response to &quot;Why has no one ever done this&quot; I&quot;m more prone to a narrative point of unintended conquenences as breaking one thing breaks another which breaks another and so on.. This is also the caveat I put on Mages undoing the Embrace they definately need to make preparations for more than &quot;Alot of Paradox&quot;(which is surmountable)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T06:01:09-08:00","id":1055612,"title":"","content":"I would think that it would be impossible to surmount 100+ points of Paradox, considering that even Archmages would die with anything above 50 points of Paradox (Archmages can only use Prime 9 to expel Paradox after they get their Paradox). While some Mage games tend to devolve into such munchkinism, this is the WtA forum, so we will respect WtA Lore. In a WtA game, trying to rewrite the prohibitions of Gaia with True Magick is a good way to end up very dead.<br /> <br /> A more interesting solution for the infertility of the Metis would be for the Metis to go to the Court of the Moon and directly petition Luna for relief. I imagine that Luna would be willing to remove the infertility of the Metis by transforming him into Human Kinfolk under two conditions. First, the Metis would have to succeed on a ridiculously difficult quest. Second, the Metis would have to convince his lady love to take on the burden of being the Garou (transforming her from a mortal into a Homid Garou). Since Luna would know that his lady love was a Mage, she would be implicitly asking for the sacrifice of the Avatar of his lady love as the price of the transformation.<br /> <br /> If the Mage is willing to make the sacrifice and the Metis succeeds on his quest, Luna would transform the Metis into Human Kinfolk, the Mage into a Homid Garou, and the Mage's Avatar into dinner. I would turn the Mage's Mage traits and the Garou's Garou traits into freebie points, sacrifice half of them (rounded up) to fuel the transformation, and allow each character to spend the remaining freebie points on traits relevant to their condition (Human Kinfolk Traits for the former Metis and Homid Garou Traits for the former Mage). Once the transformation was complete, the two lovers could have children and their story would become part of the Lore of the Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T07:54:20-08:00","id":1055652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053918-cross-genre-relationships?p=1055612#post1055612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would think that it would be impossible to surmount 100+ points of Paradox, considering that even Archmages would die with anything above 50 points of Paradox (Archmages can only use Prime 9 to expel Paradox after they get their Paradox). While some Mage games tend to devolve into such munchkinism, this is the WtA forum, so we will respect WtA Lore. In a WtA game, trying to rewrite the prohibitions of Gaia with True Magick is a good way to end up very dead.<br /> <br /> A more interesting solution for the infertility of the Metis would be for the Metis to go to the Court of the Moon and directly petition Luna for relief. I imagine that Luna would be willing to remove the infertility of the Metis by transforming him into Human Kinfolk under two conditions. First, the Metis would have to succeed on a ridiculously difficult quest. Second, the Metis would have to convince his lady love to take on the burden of being the Garou (transforming her from a mortal into a Homid Garou). Since Luna would know that his lady love was a Mage, she would be implicitly asking for the sacrifice of the Avatar of his lady love as the price of the transformation.<br /> <br /> If the Mage is willing to make the sacrifice and the Metis succeeds on his quest, Luna would transform the Metis into Human Kinfolk, the Mage into a Homid Garou, and the Mage's Avatar into dinner. I would turn the Mage's Mage traits and the Garou's Garou traits into freebie points, sacrifice half of them (rounded up) to fuel the transformation, and allow each character to spend the remaining freebie points on traits relevant to their condition (Human Kinfolk Traits for the former Metis and Homid Garou Traits for the former Mage). Once the transformation was complete, the two lovers could have children and their story would become part of the Lore of the Garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow. I am a relatively new WtA player and I know next to nothing about Mage. I had no idea any of this was even possible. I guess even a Metis can dream. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12788-ruadhan","name":"Ruadhan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T07:57:04-08:00","id":1055654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ruadhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053918-cross-genre-relationships?p=1055652#post1055652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wow. I am a relatively new WtA player and I know next to nothing about Mage. I had no idea any of this was even possible. I guess even a Metis can dream. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Or rather an ST and/or Metis player can dream. <br /> <br /> This falls under ST fiat. Not something that is part of the base setting, but one of the joys of table top RPGs is anything is possible if you can convince the ST to allow it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T08:42:12-08:00","id":1055663,"title":"","content":"Of course, but most of the epic tales fall into 'ST fiat' territory. Luna is a Celestine, so She can do almost anything, the question is convincing Her to bother. An epic quest and major sacrifices from both lovers would be suitable for my games. Other STs would have different criteria.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T10:21:23-08:00","id":1055698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ruadhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053918-cross-genre-relationships?p=1055652#post1055652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow. I am a relatively new WtA player and I know next to nothing about Mage. I had no idea any of this was even possible. I guess even a Metis can dream. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Arguably simpler (or at least more straight forward) would be to head to The Flux and make the changes yourself there. Removing your deformity there is technically possible, but prone to consequences. Removing infertility should be somewhat easier. In either case, this is no worse an idea than just trying to magick it away.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T10:45:50-08:00","id":1055709,"title":"","content":"The problem with the Flux Realm is that the Coil is whimsical in the favors that it gives shapeshifters (and I am not sure if an Incarna is powerful enough to remove a restriction set into place by Gaia, which is Celestine-level at the very least). I imagine that one solution for the Coil would be to force enough Wyld energy into a Metis so that the Wyrm Taint associated with being a Metis is burned out, which would also remove the Weaver Taint of being part-human. The Metis would be transformed into a perfectly fertile Wolf Kinfolk Gorgon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T11:17:38-08:00","id":1055716,"title":"","content":"Would I be correct to assume &quot;the Coil&quot; is an incarna they've placed in the Flux in W20? In the older Umbra books, there was just a system in place for you to make alternations to yourself once you get inside. It wasn't dependent on an outside entity to function.<br /> <br /> In any case, if anyone can make the argument that a Mage can circumvent the infertility thing, then an Incarna (of the Wyld) certainly can. That just seems like a completely logical conclusion to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T11:56:03-08:00","id":1055721,"title":"","content":"I am not disagreeing with you, I just do not think that a Mage (or anything less powerful than a Celestine) can circumvent a curse of Gaia, at least not according to the WtA Lore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T12:12:23-08:00","id":1055727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053918-cross-genre-relationships?p=1055721#post1055721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not disagreeing with you, I just do not think that a Mage (or anything less powerful than a Celestine) can circumvent a curse of Gaia, at least not according to the WtA Lore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh. That seemed to be the direction of some of the comments above, so I figured the Flux idea was worth throwing out therell. And it's more in the wheelhouse of WtA so at least there is a system in place for that sort of thing.<br /> <br /> Either way, this is the sort of stuff that generates interesting stories. Having a hope of something working (even if we know OOC that it shouldn't) tends to be better than flat out saying no.<br /> <br /> So is that what &quot;the Coil&quot; is?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T12:57:36-08:00","id":1055750,"title":"","content":"I was under the impression from what I've read that Metis cannot permanently get rid of their deformity in the Flux, that it comes back as soon as they leave that realm. Is this incorrect?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12788-ruadhan","name":"Ruadhan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T13:28:49-08:00","id":1055760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053918-cross-genre-relationships?p=1055721#post1055721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not disagreeing with you, I just do not think that a Mage (or anything less powerful than a Celestine) can circumvent a curse of Gaia, at least not according to the WtA Lore.</div> </div> </div> </div>That depends on if you interpret it as a curse from gaia. In purely werewolf cosmology it's more likely, but still a valid question. In werewolf + mage cosmology things get &quot;wyrd&quot; fast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T13:30:09-08:00","id":1055762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ruadhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053918-cross-genre-relationships?p=1055750#post1055750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was under the impression from what I've read that Metis cannot permanently get rid of their deformity in the Flux, that it comes back as soon as they leave that realm. Is this incorrect?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's ST fiat. But the infertility and the deformity are separate (though probably related). So you should be able to try for one without affecting the other. And maybe you come out fertile, but with 2 deformities. The Flux is the heart of the Wyld. Anything is possible. But that's exactly the sort of thing that ST fiat covers.<br /> <br /> Edit: Worth adding that anything that can possibly cure your Metis sterility is going to be ST fiat anyways. Are Mage shenanigans any more valid a reason than the Flux? I would say not. If your ST wants to explore this path with you than either option is at least just as valid as the other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","user":"idpersona","date":". 02-27-2017, 04:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T13:32:18-08:00","id":1055764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053918-cross-genre-relationships?p=1055473#post1055473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I think that 'Gaia says no' and the Mage gains 10,000 points of Paradox for trying to circumvent Gaia's prohibitions against Metis's reproducing (only a Supernal like the Wyrm seems to be able to avoid that fate). If Mages could just cure Metis infertility, the Garou would try to get along with Mages better. Of course, the only thing the Metis realizes is that his lady love is annihilated in an explosion that takes out a small city (assuming he was not in the vicinity)..</div> </div> </div> </div> Why would you inherently gain paradox for messing around with a spirit curse? I could understand not overcoming Gaia's power. But I'm not sure it would express itself through Paradox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T14:52:06-08:00","id":1055803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1053918-cross-genre-relationships?p=1055461#post1055461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know what I would do as ST? I think I would have the child be born a normal human. Not Kinfolk. Not Garou. Not Metis. Not crazy freak monster baby. Just a normal Delerium prone human baby.</div> </div> </div> </div>If for no other reason than the &quot;children take after their mother's breed-form&quot; bit, I also would think the kid would either be regular ol' human or potentially Kinfolk (just as if a Garou ended up with a regular ol' human woman).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12777-wakuwa","name":"Wakuwa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12777_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}